// The oak's shape. Placement is not here -- that is PHASE1_ARCHITECTURE.md
// 8.4's structure pass, which is code. This is only what a tree looks like,
// so it can be retuned without a recompile (REQUIREMENTS.md #3).
//
// `density` is "one in N chunk columns has a tree", an integer rather than a
// float on purpose: the placement decision has to be bit-identical across
// platforms (8.5), and an integer comparison is the cheapest way to be sure.
// Lower is denser.
Structure(
    name:     "cubara:oak",
    trunk:    (block: "cubara:oak_log", height: (4, 6)),
    canopy:   (block: "cubara:oak_leaves", radius: 2),
    grows_on: "cubara:grass",
    density:  12,
)
